{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Is this not that which my lord drinks from?</b> He did not mention the goblet to them explicitly, but spoke with them as though it were already known that they had taken the goblet. Therefore he said: Is this not the one you took, which my lord drinks from? They too answered as though they did not know what he was seeking: \"How could we steal from your master's house silver or gold?\" And they said, \"He with whom it is found among your servants\" — silver or gold stolen — \"shall die.\"" "And the meaning of <b>that which my lord drinks from</b> is a fabrication, to magnify their guilt upon them, for one who steals the king's cup from which he drinks holds the kingdom in contempt, and it will not avail him even if he multiplies bribe and restitution." "<b>And he indeed divines with it.</b> For he does not want his cup to be for others, and he inquired of the diviners concerning it. And this is what he said, \"a man such as me\" — and his intention is to say that through the divination he knew that they stole it, and therefore he pursued them more than all who come into his house. And all this was to disguise himself in the matter, just as he disguised himself when he searched, beginning with the eldest and ending with the youngest, to completion."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:27.790662945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}